      "content": "Using a thick layer of standard antibiotic ointment like Neosporin is generally acceptable for minor burns *after* the initial cooling phase, as it can help keep the area moist and prevent infection. However, since you mentioned the redness is spreading and it looks deep, this suggests the burn might be more severe than you realize. For any burn that looks deep or is spreading, professional assessment is the safest course of action to ensure it heals correctly.",
